  data: {
    LLM: "Bankers should always lead their strongest non-trump suits early to force the Attackers to spend their trumps on low-value tricks.\n\nPoint Control: If you are the Attacker and know you can't win the trick, throw your point cards (5s, 10s) to your PARTNER if they are likely to win it.\n\nThe Void Tactic: Try to empty your hand of a low-value suit early so you can 'Trump In' (ruff) when that suit is led, stealing the points from the Bankers.",
    Player: "Bankers should always lead their strongest non-trump suits early to force the Attackers to spend their trumps on low-value tricks.\n\nPoint Control: If you are the Attacker and know you can't win the trick, throw your point cards (5s, 10s) to your PARTNER if they are likely to win it.\n\nThe Void Tactic: Try to empty your hand of a low-value suit early so you can 'Trump In' (ruff) when that suit is led, stealing the points from the Bankers.",
